.TH ORCA\-WATCHDOG 1 "2026-09-10" "orca-watchdog 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
orca\-watchdog \- auto\-resume rate\-limited or stalled Orca terminals
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B orca\-watchdog
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B orca\-watchdog
is a macOS
.BR launchd (8)
user agent that watches every connected Orca terminal for a stalled agent TUI
and sends a resume prompt only when it is safe to. It resumes after a stated
rate\-limit reset, and after an API outage once the relevant status page reports
recovery. It never touches a terminal that is busy, that is waiting on user
input, or that was deliberately stopped, and it holds instead of guessing
whenever a check is inconclusive.
.PP
The watchdog installs
.BR stopped .
Nothing is registered with
.BR launchd (8)
and no terminal is ever touched until you explicitly run
.BR "orca\-watchdog start" .
Once started,
.BR launchd (8)
runs one observation tick every 5 minutes.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Check macOS, Node, the Orca CLI, the
.BR launchd (8)
job, pause flag, and event state, and print specific recovery commands.
Read\-only: it never repairs, restarts, registers, or sends.
.TP
.B start
Validate the environment, then register the LaunchAgent. Resolves absolute paths
to Node and the Orca CLI at this point.
.TP
.B stop
Unregister the LaunchAgent. Stored state is retained.
.TP
.B pause
Disable all watchdog activity without unregistering or deleting state.
.TP
.B resume
Re\-enable watchdog activity after a
.BR pause .
.TP
.B status
Show service health, pause state, the installed version, the last completed
check, the last successful resume, and any pending events with the latest
waiting reason.
.TP
.B logs
Print the most recent activity, read\-only. See
.B LOGS
below for options.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Run one observation\-only tick and report what it would do. Never sends terminal
input and never writes state.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a usage summary.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the installed version.
.SH LOGS
.B orca\-watchdog logs
prints the latest 100 activity lines by default. It is read\-only and never
rotates or truncates a log.
.TP
.B \-\-follow
Follow the log as it grows, reprinting from the tail across truncation or
replacement. Interrupt with Ctrl\-C.
.TP
.BI \-\-lines " N"
Show the last
.I N
lines instead of 100.
.I N
must be a positive integer.
.TP
.BI \-\-source " activity|stdout|stderr"
Choose the stream:
.B activity
(the watchdog's own log, the default),
.B stdout
or
.B stderr
(the
.BR launchd (8)
job output). A missing log file reads as empty, which is normal before the
first tick.
.SH INSTALLATION
Homebrew (recommended). Add the tap, trust it (newer Homebrew requires trusting
third\-party taps), then install:
.PP
.RS
.EX
brew tap johncioni/tap
brew trust johncioni/tap
brew install johncioni/tap/orca\-watchdog
.EE
.RE
.PP
Homebrew installs Node for you. The archive install requires Node.js 22 or newer
already on
.BR PATH ;
extract the release and run
.B ./install.sh
from the extracted directory, which stages the version under
.I ~/.local/share/orca\-watchdog/<version>/
and links the command into
.IR ~/.local/bin/orca\-watchdog .
.PP
After installing, start the service explicitly:
.PP
.RS
.EX
orca\-watchdog doctor
orca\-watchdog start
.EE
.RE
.SH UPGRADES
Always stop before upgrading, then verify and start again. Homebrew:
.PP
.RS
.EX
orca\-watchdog stop
brew upgrade johncioni/tap/orca\-watchdog
orca\-watchdog doctor && orca\-watchdog start
.EE
.RE
.PP
Archive: stop, run the new archive's
.BR ./install.sh " (it keeps the previous version for rollback), then"
.BR doctor " and " start "."
If a new version misbehaves, roll back with
.B ./install.sh \-\-rollback
and start again.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B orca\-watchdog doctor
is the first stop for any problem: it reports macOS, Node, Orca CLI, and
.BR launchd (8)
state, flags missing targets, stale runtime versions, and disagreement between
the saved plist and the loaded job, and prints the exact recovery commands.
A deliberately stopped service is reported as a valid state, not an error.
Malformed event or health metadata is diagnosed read\-only and never rewritten.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/orca\-watchdog/
State and logs (owner\-only):
.I state.json
(event state),
.I health.json
(operational health),
.I disabled
(pause flag),
.I watchdog.log
(activity),
.I launchd.out.log
and
.I launchd.err.log
.RB ( launchd (8)
output).
.TP
.I ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.john.orca\-watchdog.plist
The LaunchAgent definition written by
.BR start .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/orca\-watchdog/
Archive install root, with
.I current
and
.I previous
version symlinks.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ORCA_CLI
Path to the Orca CLI when
.B orca
is not on
.BR PATH .
.TP
.B ORCA_WATCHDOG_NODE
Explicit Node binary for the launcher. The Homebrew wrapper sets this to
Homebrew's Node.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success;
.B 1
on a runtime error or a failing
.BR doctor " check;"
.B 2
for an unknown command or invalid option.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR launchd (8),
.BR launchctl (1).
The project README documents detection, sends, and troubleshooting in full.
